{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat R9-BRIEF.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-13 07:1x GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-13 14:1x +0700\nCoding-Agent: codex (jupiter POOL 2 — the expiring meter; draw it down)\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated — fresh thread; the terra authoring thread lives on the laptop and cannot resume here)\n\n# Task: D1 continuation r9 (jupiter) — finalize the bounds declaration, the tagged verification run, and the verification-result publication\n\nRole: VM Engineer (compiler provenance)\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-terra | Assigned: 2026-11-13 14:1x +0700 | Status: active | Rationale: the owner directs jupiter's POOL 2 codex be drawn down before its ~4-day expiry; D1 r9 is the queued codex-shaped round. By-state resume — the worktree holds the full r1-r8 WIP.\n\n## State resume (by state — you have no prior thread context; everything is in the worktree)\n\nWorktree: `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1` (branch d1-correspondence @ `747e80fc`, the recovery-by-state WIP commit). It contains:\n- `src/cljc/yang/correspondence.cljc` + `src/cljc/yang/correspondence_text.clj` — the D1 record/recipe/profile/binding-coverage machinery (r1-r5).\n- `src/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.cljc` — the INDEPENDENT verifier (r6: own site-declaration derivation, own source-hash, own paired-tree binding reconstruction; producer-vs-verifier agreement on the pilot fixture; the mutated-declaration rejection).\n- `test/yang/correspondence_test.cljc`, `test/yang/correspondence_text_test.clj`, `test/yang/correspondence_verifier_test.cljc` — the red-first test families.\n- `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` — the capture/replay machinery + the per-fixture corpus gates.\n- `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence.edn` — NOT yet created (the companion file, r9's deliverable).\n- `collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r{1..8}*.findings.md` + `1794670000001-...partial.findings.md` + `1794671000001-d1-bounds-declaration-draft.md` — the findings chain r1-r8 and the bounds DRAFT. Read the chain first; the draft is what you finalize.\n\nThe original dispatch brief: `collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-durable-correspondence.prompt.md` (with the POST-CC3/PORT/REFACTOR amendment section). The two astra rulings that bind the design: `1794524600000-architect-d1-recipe-input-adjudication.gpt-6-astra.findings.md` (RULING (A): reconstruction from admission-captured text under the pinned profile; the normative §4.1 amendment) and `1794422563000-architect-d1-profile-amendment-r2.gpt-6-astra.findings.md` (RULING (b): the numeric-fidelity relation — equal-valued Byte/Short/Integer/Long interchange, BigInt/Ratio/BigDecimal/Double class identity, the NaN clause; the profile versioning requirement).\n\n## Environment\n\nThis is JUPITER (`jupiter.stigmergy.systems`), POOL 2 of the codex quota (the independent meter the owner wants drawn down). The worktree's mise.toml was trusted and ANTLR prerequisites generated by the orchestrator (`build/antlr` populated). `bb` is available via `export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$HOME/.local/share/mise/shims:/snap/bin:$PATH\"` + `eval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"` (mise trusted). If any prerequisite is missing, self-heal with that PATH + `mise trust` + `bb gen:antlr` / `bb deps:npm`.\n\n## The work (r9 — three deliverables in order)\n\n1. **Finalize the bounds declaration** (`1794671000001-d1-bounds-declaration-draft.md` is the draft; the cc3 v2 declaration `1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md` is the format precedent): the draft's storage/rows/sites/elapsed ceilings came from the LAPTOP corpus run — re-measure the peak-heap and lane quantities on THIS host (jupiter) per the draft's own \"NOT declared — r9 must measure\" clause, declare the finite ceilings from measured data with headroom, max-based pass/fail, and record the jupiter-scoped declaration as the run's of-record bounds.\n2. **The tagged verification run UNDER the declaration**: the independent verifier (`yang.correspondence-verifier`) executes the scoped attribution query over BOTH C lanes for the corpus fixtures — the design §4.2 step 6 — with the declaration's ceilings enforced (max-based pass/fail; a ceiling exceedance is a failed bounded run, never a raised ceiling). The run consumes the persisted record/inputs from the r8 machinery. Red-first for any gate machinery you add.\n3. **The verification-result publication**: the separate result record (design §4.2 step 7) — the record's address, the verifier revision, the inputs, per-fixture outcomes, the tagged-run evidence — published as `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_verification.edn` (the design's named artifact; the cc3 v2-declaration precedent governs the format) or a sibling path if the design's exact name conflicts with existing files. Plus the companion file `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence.edn` (the corpus record per r2/r3's construction, with the retention manifest note from r7 — the OWNER DECISION on the retention location is pending; construct the record and store it in the worktree's scratch store, and note the pending decision; do NOT commit the 700 MiB store).\n\n## Bounds/invariants/deliverable\n\nThe bounded file list from the original brief + this amendment; forbidden set unchanged (`slice9_site_tables.edn` bytes frozen — SHA `e435ac40...` per the r2 inventory; no canonical surfaces; no macro.cljc/semantic.cljc/ast_walker.cljc/clojure.cljc/core-prelude/dht.cljc). Origins only from retained coordinates (the rebind note `1794519755000-...findings.md` item 3 pins the post-port mechanics). The verifier rejects, never substitutes (`:trusted` is not verification). Red-first per item; the standing nets stay green (`yang.correspondence-test`, `yang.clojure-callsite-test`); kondo 0 errors. The full oracle suite is shiva-scale — do NOT run it here.\n\nDeliverable: `collab/yang-clojure/1794698000000-engineer-d1-r9-jupiter.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md` (worktree mirror; the orchestrator promotes). Include: the jupiter-scoped bounds declaration (final), the tagged-run evidence, the verification-result record, per-fixture outcomes, and any DEFECT or refusal with its stage. Commit NOTHING.\n\nIf the tagged run exceeds a ceiling: record the exceedance honestly (a failed bounded run) and deliver the partial — never raise a ceiling silently.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS local-timezone-name>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
